  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 356 PM EDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nWhile we will remain under northwest flow aloft, the upper ridge to \nthe west weakens and flattens allowing us to cool off a bit and see \nlower dew points in the 60s and highs in the mid/upper 80s. This \nperiod looks to be mainly dry through the end of the week. \n\nOur next chance for precipitation appears to be this weekend as a \nshortwave trough will work over the northern peripheral of the \nwestern ridge and then moves into the Ohio Valley. Deterministic \nmodels then have this shortwave getting cutoff over the region for \nearly next week.",
